#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:5
#: 853c062732fe43a1b73278afa930b9b4
msgid "LOITER Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:7
#: cef0170c74ae4cc585fbcfd52d9b508c
msgid "In LOITER mode the plane will circle around the point where you started the loiter, holding altitude at the altitude that you entered loiter in. The radius of the circle is controlled by the ``WP_LOITER_RAD`` parameter, but is also limited by your ``NAV_ROLL_CD`` limit, and your ``NAVL1_PERIOD`` navigation tuning. As with :ref:`Return To Launch (RTL) <rtl-mode>` and :ref:`AUTO <auto-mode>` mode you can \"nudge\" the plane while in LOITER using stick mixing, if enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:15
#: a869247e5c294ab99a8c1f3a3442a253
msgid "If :ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` bit 12 is set (+4096 to value) and :ref:`STICK_MIXING<STICK_MIXING>` is set to 1, then altitude of the loiter can be changed using the pitch stick, as in FBWB mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:19
#: 2a04ee191c4f49ea9ba815d9f398d7ec
msgid "\"Home\" position is always supposed to be your Plane's actual GPS takeoff location:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:22
#: b989f481ad95421185dcebfbaebde490
msgid "It is very important to acquire GPS lock before arming in order for RTL, Loiter, Auto or any GPS dependent mode to work properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:24
#: 4085c72c913d4e1691c13a778e23b206
msgid "For Plane the home position is initially established at the time the plane acquires its GPS lock. It is then continuously updated as long as the autopilot is disarmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:28
#: af1cb0f35f1c41f2ab428d1ff5419804
msgid "This means if you execute an RTL in Plane, it will return to the location where it was when it was armed - assuming it had acquired GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/loiter-mode.rst:29
#: aae3d963b6bb4f9581bfc5e75dfcedff
msgid "Consider the use of :ref:`Rally Points <common-rally-points>` to avoid returning directly to your arming point on RTL."
msgstr ""
